> A cliff penalty returns to the start

From the bottom-left start, moving right hits the cliff: reward-100, state36 again, and no terminal flag. Moving up then pays-1 and reaches state24. The cliff is a costly transition, not an absorbing loss state.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/grid_world_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");e::CliffWalking env;env.reset(1);auto a=env.step(1);auto c=env.step(0);std::vector<double>values{a.reward,a.obs[0],double(a.terminated),c.reward,c.obs[0]};if(a.reward!=-100||a.obs[0]!=36||a.terminated||c.obs[0]!=24)return 1;std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/grid_world_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);const double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1e-9,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).title("A cliff penalty returns to the start").x_label("Coordinate in displayed calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/grid_world_worked.svg");}
